Make key-granted Pro permanent, and let friends see each other's progress

The Lemon Squeezy webhook wrote isPro unconditionally on every subscription
event. An account that redeemed a key and later took out -- then cancelled --
a subscription would be set back to free by an unrelated billing event, and
because a key can only be spent once and redeemedKey is pinned, that account
could never get its Pro back. Founder and comp accounts would have quietly
lost access with no way to restore it.

Redemption now stamps proSource: 'key' and the webhook refuses to revoke Pro
that came from a key. proSource is pinned as hard as redeemedKey -- if it
could be cleared, the protection it grants could be cleared with it, which is
the same shape of bug closed this morning.

On Daniel's question: creating and joining a room go through the SAME socket
event, which has verified the plan server-side since this morning, so joining
was already Pro. But he was right that something is broken -- the FREE friends
feature had nothing free to do. A friend row offered Message (free) and Study
together (a Pro room), and neither of the two things named as free -- challenge
each other, see each other's progress -- existed at all.

Friends can now see each other's level, XP and streak. A separate collection
rather than more fields on /users: that document holds email, plan, token spend
and redeemed keys, and loosening its rule to expose a level would have exposed
everything beside it. user_stats holds four numbers, enforced with hasOnly.
Read access goes through the friendship document itself using the same
sorted-pair id, so unfriending closes the window on the next read.

Proved against the DEPLOYED rules with throwaway accounts: key grant survives,
proSource cannot be cleared (403), a stranger cannot read stats (403), a friend
can (200), nobody can write someone else's (403), and after unfriending the
friend is refused (403). All nine checks passed; test data deleted.

Also removes commitmsg.txt, which the previous commit picked up by accident.

192 tests passing (8 new), tsc clean, build clean, rules deployed.

